#!/usr/bin/env node
// check-contrast.js — the gate that would have caught brilliant-on-grey.
//
// 2026-10-14: PN02 shipped brilliant-green (#00D639) icons on a light-grey
// (#F2F5F6) stripe at 1.8:1 — invisible to every existing gate (copy sync,
// bindings, sync-check, and verify-section all passed: the classes were
// right, the ASSET color was wrong). This gate pins icon-asset fills and
// text colors against the stripe background as WCAG ratios, in a real
// browser, from the same terms.json oracle the other tools use.
//
// WHAT IT CHECKS (per component `figma/terms.json` `theme` block):
//   icons: every fill painted by the section's SVG assets vs the computed
//     stripe background, min 3.0 (WCAG 1.4.11 non-text graphics)
//   texts: every listed selector's computed color vs background, min 4.5
//     (WCAG 1.4.3 normal text; alpha is blended over the bg first)
// A theme change (dark<->light) must move bg + icons + text together; any
// one left behind fails loudly here instead of shipping quietly.
//
// USAGE
//   node tooling/check-contrast.js --selftest

